course: dictionary
lesson: 8612
title: Scratchy: rough, harsh or sore
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which meaning fits. «Scratchy» is a good example, so look at the context before you choose.
explain: «Scratchy» can describe cloth that feels rough and makes your skin itch, like a wool jumper. It can also describe a sound or voice that is harsh and crackly, like an old record.
explain: «Tired, dry or scratchy eyes are a sign that you need rest and sleep.» Here scratchy means sore and dry, not rough. Try the meaning in the sentence: does it still make sense? It does, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Scratchy is an adjective, so it describes a noun, as in a scratchy jumper.
fact: Scratchy can describe a scratchy throat, which feels sore and dry.
fact: Scratchy can also mean rough, harsh or crackly, like an old record.
fact: Scratchy writing or drawing is made of rough, untidy lines.
fact: The forms are scratchy, scratchier and scratchiest.
exercise: Lena's new jumper is «scratchy», so she wears a t-shirt underneath. What does scratchy mean? | Very long | Bright red | *Rough and makes your skin itch | Soft and warm
exercise: «The old radio gave a scratchy, crackly voice.» What does scratchy describe? | A cold drink | *A harsh, crackly sound | A smooth, quiet sound | A sunny day
exercise: Which sentence uses scratchy to mean sore and dry? | *«Ali's throat felt scratchy when he woke up.» | «The scratchy record played his favourite song.» | «The scratchy jumper was warm and soft.»
test: In «a scratchy old record», what does scratchy mean? | Smooth and quiet | Brand new | *Rough, harsh and crackly | Very cold
test: What does a scratchy throat feel like? | Cool and wet | Full of music | *Sore and dry | Soft as silk
exam: Which word means the same as scratchy in «Theo's eyes felt scratchy and dry after a late game»? | Shiny and smooth | *Sore and dry | Loud and happy | Warm and wet
